     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Initiated sub-national systems leadership programme based on capacity needs assessment.
2. Engaged two off-takers to demonstrate initial public-private-community collaboration and partnerships to strengthen sustainable production and sustainable value chains for selected agricultural commodities.
3. Conducted ESIA and SESA, and development of the ESMP management plan.
4. Conducted project inception workshop and reporting.
5. Conducted project board and steering committee meetings as well as annual stakeholders workshop
6. Operational of the PMU including hired key technical experts.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">There is no concrete project/output level result has been achieved yet during this PAR Reporting period. Project document was signed in 21 February 2022, and the Inception Workshop was conducted by end of August 2022, followed by series of coordination and landscape verification process in five districts under five provinces through multistakeholder and inclusive process. The project has been involved in several online activities with the Global FOLUR team. The objectives are to: 1) increase knowledge and exchange learning on the topic related to green commodities and gender aspect of the Food Agriculture and Commodity System; 2) Building coordination and networking with the global FOLUR team. 
Through these activities, the project FOLUR Indonesia team has been trained on several aspects related to managing the project related to green commodities, including building trust with stakeholders and adaptive learning. The network has also been established with the global FOLUR Team, which can provide technical support and advice as relevant for successful FOLUR project implementation, including gender approach to project implementation which has been tailored to FACS approach.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
